course: dictionary
lesson: 14509
title: Sorry, and showing it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Penitent is a word for someone who is truly sorry for doing wrong. Look at the clues around it: a penitent person says sorry, looks sorry and wants to put things right. «Sam looked penitent after he broke the window.» Sam is sorry, and his face and body show it.
explain: Penitent can describe a person, a face, or a voice. «She gave a penitent smile and picked up the broken cup.» Here the smile is not happy. It shows that she feels sorry and wants to make up for the accident.
explain: In old church stories, a penitent is a person who owns up to their wrongs and asks for forgiveness. In the story of the Prodigal Son, the father welcomes back his penitent son. The son has admitted his mistakes and wants to change.
fact: Penitent means feeling and showing that you are sorry for doing wrong.
fact: Penitent is an adjective: you can say «a penitent sinner», «penitent tears» or «look penitent».
fact: In church, a penitent is a person who confesses their sins to a priest or does penance.
fact: In the Prodigal Son story, the father welcomes back his penitent son.
fact: Penitent goes further than just saying sorry: it shows sorrow and a wish to make things right.
exercise: «Sam looked penitent after he broke the window.» What does penitent mean? | *Feeling sorry for doing wrong | Feeling bored and sleepy | Feeling cold on a winter day | Feeling very proud of a good deed
exercise: «The penitent boy hugged his sister and promised never to lie again.» Which clue shows he is penitent? | *He hugged his sister and promised never to lie again | He laughed loudly at a joke | He ate all the cake quickly | He ran outside to play
exercise: In old church stories, what is a penitent? | A priest who lights the candles | A child who goes to bed early | A person who sings in the church choir | *A person who owns up to their wrongs and asks for forgiveness
test: Which word is closest in meaning to penitent? | *Sorry | Bored | Excited | Angry
test: Which sentence shows a penitent person? | Mia laughed and ran off to the park. | *Mia said sorry, bowed her head and promised to tidy her room. | Mia ate three biscuits and smiled. | Mia counted the stars in the sky.
exam: The father welcomed back his ___ son with open arms. | sleepy | cheerful | *penitent | hungry
